input.command:
S=/c/Users/VNasher/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c1b810ae341cf89c/38d5d26e-8eba-4a4b-8a8d-b9f20f94200f/scratchpad && cat > $S/v06.js <<'EOF'
const fs=require('fs');const p=process.argv[2];let t=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');
function r(a,b){if(t.split(a).length!==2)throw new Error('not unique: '+a.slice(0,60));t=t.split(a).join(b);}
r('**v0.5, 2026-11-12** — owner\'s vision plus four rounds','**v0.6, 2026-11-12** — owner\'s vision plus five rounds');
r('## Changelog\n','## Changelog\n- v0.6 (2026-11-12): art rule clarified for characters (style of the world they belong to); story premise; opening sequence with the first gun; starting spells; enchant only with a gun in hand; key changes (F quick-use, G interact, L1 enchant on gamepad); counter-style ammo refilled on era travel; automatic checkpoints; no sprint; one full-armor slot.\n');
r('- **The rule follows the object, not the era.** A 3D gun stays 3D in the past; a pixel-art fireball stays pixel art in the future.\n',
'- **The rule follows the object, not the era.** A 3D gun stays 3D in the past; a pixel-art fireball stays pixel art in the future.\n- **Characters take the style of the world they belong to.** An orc of the castle is a classic pixel-art fantasy orc (80s, 90s, early 2000s games). An orc of the future is a 3D, heavily armored sci-fi orc. They are different enemies, not the same orc in two styles.\n');
r(`### Opening sequence
1. The player starts in the **medieval castle** (past) with a **staff and spells**.
2. Kills a **small group of orcs**.
3. **Interacts with an object** → **short, simple cutscene #1**.
4. Appears in the **future**.
5. Fights **armed orcs**.
6. **Short cutscene #2.**
7. Rest of the game: **TBD**.
- A third, separate map unlocks late: a **dimension between space and time** where the true final boss lives (see §11).`,
`- A third, separate map unlocks late: a **dimension between space and time** where the true final boss lives (see §11).

### Story premise
- The player is a **mage** who travels to the castle out of **curiosity**: he had heard it was a mysterious place.
- On reaching the **seal** in the castle he is **trapped** and thrown into the future.
- In the future he hears **a woman's voice asking for help**. That voice is his reason to fix the problem.
- Cutscenes: **few and short**, each one written for its situation.

### Opening sequence
1. The player starts in the **medieval castle** (past) with a **staff and the starting spells** (§6).
2. Kills a **small group of pixel-art orcs**.
3. **Interacts with the seal** → **short cutscene #1** (trapped, sent forward in time).
4. Appears in the **future**.
5. Fights **3D armed orcs**. One of the first ones **drops the first gun**.
6. The player **picks up the gun** → **short cutscene #2**. The player **cannot progress** without picking it up.
7. Rest of the game: **TBD**.`);
r('- **Air passives are always active**: they are not equipped and do not take a slot.\n',
'- **Air passives are always active**: they are not equipped and do not take a slot.\n- **Starting spells:** Fireball (very early tier), Lightning bolt (early tier), Ice wall. The other spells: see open questions.\n');
r(`### Weapon enchant (always equipped)
- A spell that **cannot be unequipped**.`,`### Weapon enchant (always equipped)
- A spell that **cannot be unequipped**.
- **Only usable with a gun in hand** (it enchants the gun).`);
r('- Staff in hand: basic magic attack + the 5 spells + the enchant. Gun in hand: shoot + aim + reload + the enchant only.',
'- Staff in hand: basic magic attack + the 5 spells. Gun in hand: shoot + aim + reload + the enchant.');
r(`- **Magazines and reload**, like any shooter.
- **Limited ammo**, picked up from the floor where enemies drop it.`,
`- **Magazines and reload**, like any shooter.
- **Ammo works like classic tactical shooters:** each gun has a fixed number of spare magazines, and each magazine a fixed number of bullets.
- **All ammo refills completely every time the player travels between eras.**
- Between refills, ammo is **picked up from the floor** where enemies drop it.
- Level design keeps ammo tight: never infinite, never starving.`);
r('- Known effect: some armor changes the QTE time-slow amount (§7). Other stats, slots and how it is equipped: **TBD**.',
'- **One armor slot = one full armor.** No separate helmet, arms or chest pieces.\n- Known effect: some armor changes the QTE time-slow amount (§7). Other stats: **TBD**.');
r('| Primary attack (staff: basic magic attack; gun: shoot) | Left click | **TBD** |','| Primary attack (staff: basic magic attack; gun: shoot) | Left click | R2 / RT |');
r('| Aim (gun in hand) | Right click | **TBD** |','| Aim (gun in hand) | Right click | L2 / LT |');
r('| Weapon enchant (any held weapon) | T (R is reload) | L2 + R2 together (LT + RT) — see open question 1 |','| Weapon enchant (gun in hand only) | T (R is reload) | L1 / LB (free with a gun in hand) |');
r('| Quick-use item (grenade / potion / injection share one slot) | **TBD** | **TBD** |','| Quick-use item (grenade / potion / injection share one slot) | F | **TBD** |');
r('| Interact (chests, portals, objects) | F | Triangle (Y) |','| Interact (chests, portals, objects) | G | Triangle (Y) |');
r('Right click means "spell slot 1" with the staff and "aim" with a gun; the two never clash because spells cannot be cast with a gun in hand.',
'Right click / L1 change meaning with the held weapon and never clash: staff = spell slot 1; gun = aim (right click) and enchant (L1). L2 means "spell modifier" with the staff and "aim" with a gun.\n\nNo sprint (the air speed passive covers movement speed).');
r('- On death the player **returns to the last checkpoint**.','- On death the player **returns to the last checkpoint**. Checkpoints are **automatic**.');
fs.writeFileSync(p,t);
EOF
node $S/v06.js Design/GDD.md && echo ok

