r("**v0.6, 2026-11-12** — owner's vision plus five rounds","**v0.7, 2026-11-12** — owner's vision plus six rounds");
r('## Changelog\n','## Changelog\n- v0.7 (2026-11-12): full story (the entity, the false voice, the Valkyrie); elemental zones in the castle unlock the rest of each element; air passives learned the same way; shotgun and rifle dropped by enemies; era travel restores everything (bonfire-like); remaining keys confirmed.\n');
r('- **Nothing is lost when changing era.** Health, mana, ammo, inventory, spells and weapons all carry over. Mana exists and works in the future; guns work in the past.\n',
'- **Nothing is lost when changing era.** Health, mana, ammo, inventory, spells and weapons all carry over. Mana exists and works in the future; guns work in the past.\n- **Era travel restores everything** (health, mana, ammo), a bit like the rest points of classic action RPGs. Portals are the safe points of the map.\n');
r(`### Story premise
- The player is a **mage** who travels to the castle out of **curiosity**: he had heard it was a mysterious place.
- On reaching the **seal** in the castle he is **trapped** and thrown into the future.
- In the future he hears **a woman's voice asking for help**. That voice is his reason to fix the problem.
- Cutscenes: **few and short**, each one written for its situation.`,
`### Story
- The player is a **mage** who travels to the castle out of **curiosity**: he had heard it was a mysterious place.
- On reaching the **seal** in the castle he is **trapped** and thrown into the future.
- In the future he hears **a woman's voice asking for help**. That voice is his reason to fix the problem.
- **The twist:** the voice is **not the Valkyrie**. It is **the Entity**, the true final boss, pretending to be her.
- **The Entity:** a fusion of an **apocalyptic artificial intelligence** and a **ghost that embodies disease**. It is locked in the dimension between space and time and wants out. To escape it needs two things: someone to **open the portal** and a **physical body to possess**.
- **The Valkyrie:** someone the Entity **manipulated across time**. The plan failed, and she ended up **trapped in both eras** (runes in the past, cryogenic tube in the future).
- **What the player does:** defeats the Valkyrie in both eras, gathers what is needed, and opens the portal: **exactly the Entity's plan**. The player walks in with the body it wants to possess. The only thing the Entity did not plan for: **the player beats it**.
- Cutscenes: **few and short**, each one written for its situation.`);
r('7. Rest of the game: **TBD**.','7. Rest of the game: elemental zones in the castle (§6), the two Valkyrie fights, the final portal (§11). Exact order and map flow: **TBD**.');
r('- **Starting spells:** Fireball (very early tier), Lightning bolt (early tier), Ice wall. The other spells: see open questions.\n',
`- **Starting spells:** Fireball (very early tier), Lightning bolt (early tier), Ice wall.

### Learning the other spells: elemental zones
- The **medieval castle** has **elemental zones**, one per element.
- Each zone has a **challenge**: a wave, a sub-boss or a boss.
- After the challenge the player gets the element's **knowledge** (from a chest, a book or similar) and **unlocks the missing spells of that element** (fire: fire wall + flamethrower; lightning: rune trap + static ball; ice: ice shield + ice floor).
- **Air passives** are learned the same way, in the air zone.
- The spell tree then upgrades what the player knows.
`);
r('- Pistol, shotgun, assault rifle.\n','- Pistol, shotgun, assault rifle.\n- The **first gun** is dropped by one of the first armed orcs in the future (§4). The **shotgun and the rifle** are dropped later by enemies, picked up from the floor.\n');
r('| Switch staff ↔ gun (↔ sword) | Mouse wheel or Alt | D-pad arrow (**TBD** which) |','| Switch staff ↔ gun (↔ sword) | Mouse wheel or Alt | D-pad up |');
r('| Quick-use item (grenade / potion / injection share one slot) | F | **TBD** |','| Quick-use item (grenade / potion / injection share one slot) | F | R1 / RB |');
r('| Cycle the quick-use item | Shift | D-pad |','| Cycle the quick-use item | Shift | D-pad left / right |');
